# Next.js App Router - Routing & Pages

## Route File Structure

Route files in `app/` must be **thin** - composition only, no business logic.

### Page Template

```typescript
// app/[page]/page.tsx
import type { Metadata } from 'next'
import { Component1, Component2 } from '@/shared/components/marketing'

export const metadata: Metadata = {
  title: 'Page Title',
  description: 'Page description for SEO',
}

export default function PageName() {
  return (
    <main>
      <Component1 {...data1} />
      <Component2 {...data2} />
    </main>
  )
}
```

## DO's and DON'Ts

### ✅ DO

```typescript
// ✅ Import components from shared or features
import { HeroCentered } from '@/shared/components/marketing'

// ✅ Define data objects inline or in separate data file
const heroData = {
  headline: "Build Better",
  subtitle: "Ship faster",
  buttons: [{ text: "Start", href: "#" }]
}

// ✅ Compose components
export default function Page() {
  return (
    <main>
      <HeroCentered {...heroData} />
    </main>
  )
}

// ✅ Use Server Components by default (no 'use client')
// ✅ Set metadata for SEO
export const metadata: Metadata = { ... }
```

### ❌ DON'T

```typescript
// ❌ NO state in route files
'use client'
const [data, setData] = useState()

// ❌ NO business logic
export default function Page() {
  const processedData = complexCalculation() // NO!
  useEffect(() => { ... }) // NO!
  
  // ❌ NO direct API calls in route component
  const data = await fetch('/api') // NO! Use in component or server action
  
  return <main>...</main>
}

// ❌ NO inline component definitions
export default function Page() {
  const InlineComponent = () => <div>...</div> // NO!
  return <main><InlineComponent /></main>
}
```

## Metadata Configuration

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT: Export metadata for SEO
export const metadata: Metadata = {
  title: 'Page Title',
  description: 'Compelling description for search engines',
  openGraph: {
    title: 'Page Title',
    description: 'OG description',
    images: ['/og-image.jpg'],
  },
}

// ✅ CORRECT: Dynamic metadata
export async function generateMetadata(): Promise<Metadata> {
  return {
    title: 'Dynamic Title',
    description: 'Dynamic description',
  }
}
```

## Layout Files

Root layout in [app/layout.tsx](mdc:app/layout.tsx):

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT: Root layout structure
import type { Metadata } from 'next'
import { Header } from '@/shared/components/layout/Header'
import { Footer } from '@/shared/components/layout/Footer'
import '@/styles/globals.css'

export const metadata: Metadata = {
  title: {
    template: '%s | Your Site',
    default: 'Your Site',
  },
  description: 'Site description',
}

export default function RootLayout({
  children,
}: {
  children: React.ReactNode
}) {
  return (
    <html lang="en">
      <body>
        <Header />
        {children}
        <Footer />
      </body>
    </html>
  )
}
```

## Route Organization

```
app/
├── layout.tsx              # Root layout
├── page.tsx                # Homepage (/)
├── about/
│   └── page.tsx           # About page (/about)
├── pricing/
│   └── page.tsx           # Pricing page (/pricing)
└── blog/
    ├── page.tsx           # Blog index (/blog)
    └── [slug]/
        └── page.tsx       # Blog post (/blog/post-slug)
```

## When to Use Client Components

Add `'use client'` ONLY in the component file that needs it, not in route files:

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG: 'use client' in route file
'use client'
export default function Page() { ... }

// ✅ CORRECT: Create interactive component separately
// features/contact/components/ContactForm/index.tsx
'use client'
export function ContactForm() {
  const [email, setEmail] = useState('')
  // Interactive logic here
}

// app/contact/page.tsx (Server Component)
import { ContactForm } from '@/features/contact/components/ContactForm'
export default function ContactPage() {
  return <main><ContactForm /></main>
}
```

## Data Loading Patterns

### Server Components (Default)

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT: Async Server Component
export default async function Page() {
  const data = await fetchData() // Runs on server
  
  return (
    <main>
      <Component data={data} />
    </main>
  )
}
```

### Client Components (Interactive)

```typescript
// In separate component file with 'use client'
'use client'
export function InteractiveComponent() {
  const [data, setData] = useState()
  
  useEffect(() => {
    fetchData().then(setData)
  }, [])
  
  return <div>{/* Use data */}</div>
}
```

## Marketing Page Pattern

For marketing/landing pages:

```typescript
// app/product/page.tsx
import type { Metadata } from 'next'
import { 
  HeroCentered, 
  FeaturesGrid, 
  PricingSimple, 
  TestimonialsGrid,
  CTASimple 
} from '@/shared/components/marketing'

export const metadata: Metadata = {
  title: 'Product',
  description: 'Product page description',
}

export default function ProductPage() {
  return (
    <main>
      <HeroCentered {...heroData} />
      <FeaturesGrid {...featuresData} />
      <PricingSimple {...pricingData} />
      <TestimonialsGrid {...testimonialsData} />
      <CTASimple {...ctaData} />
    </main>
  )
}

// Data can be in same file or imported
const heroData = { /* ... */ }
const featuresData = { /* ... */ }
// etc.
```

