## Error Handling

```typescript
// app/error.tsx
'use client'

export default function Error({
  error,
  reset,
}: {
  error: Error & { digest?: string }
  reset: () => void
}) {
  return (
    <div>
      <h2>Something went wrong!</h2>
      <button onClick={() => reset()}>Try again</button>
    </div>
  )
}
```

## Loading States

```typescript
// app/loading.tsx
export default function Loading() {
  return <div>Loading...</div>
}
```

## Key Principles

1. **Keep route files thin** - only composition
2. **Use Server Components by default** - better performance
3. **Set metadata** for every page - SEO important
4. **Import from @/ paths** - always use aliases
5. **No business logic** in route files
6. **Compose from features** - route files just assemble

See [ARCHITECTURE.md](mdc:ARCHITECTURE.md) for complete architecture details.
